<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/062E">Example <span data-tag="062E">9.2.2.5</span>.</a> If $K$ is a $\kappa $-small simplicial set, then the limit functor $\varprojlim : \operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ is $\kappa $-finitary: this is a refomulation of Theorem <a data-tag="05Y0" href="/tag/05Y0">9.1.5.9</a> (see Proposition <a data-tag="05XH" href="/tag/05XH">7.7.7.1</a>). In particular, if $K$ is a finite simplicial set, then the functor $\varprojlim : \operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ is finitary. </p>
